    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266">

                <pb facs="0335" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.911/9–2547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Argentina
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-01T18:00:00-05:00">October 1, 1947—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>921. UP reps here have requested Secretary send
                    brief statement to <hi rendition="#italic">La Prensa</hi><anchor n="45"
                        xml:id="d266-f1"/> Buenos Aires occasion 78th anniversary Oct 18. Apparently
                    that newspaper plans special anniversary edition including statements and
                    letters prominent persons many countries. Understood this customary with <hi
                        rendition="#italic">La Prensa</hi>.</p>
                <p>Pls deliver in your discretion following message from Secretary Marshall to Dr.
                    Gainza Paz, publisher <hi rendition="#italic">La Prensa:</hi>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Please accept my congratulations on the occasion of <hi
                                rendition="#italic">La Prensa’s</hi> 78th anniversary. The prestige
                            which your paper has achieved through its continued maintenance of the
                            highest standards of journalism reserves for it a special place among
                            the great newspapers of the world. I take this opportunity to wish <hi
                                rendition="#italic">La Prensa</hi> many more years of distinguished
                            public service.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d266-f1" n="45" xml:id="d266-f1-content">
                <p>This request was made by Harry W. Frantz, Foreign Department, United Press
                    Associations, in a letter of September 25 to the Assistant Secretary of State
                    for Political Affairs (Armour) (835.911/9–2547).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
